# STIG RHEL-09-672050: RHEL 9 must implement DOD-approved encryption in the bind package.
# STIG ID: V-258242 (HIGH)

META
    esp_id `r9-rhel-09-672050-crypto-policy-modules-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `rocky9`
    criticality `critical`

    title `STIG RHEL-09-672050: RHEL 9 must implement DOD-approved encryption in the bind package.`
    description `RHEL 9 must implement DOD-approved encryption in the bind package.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `rhel9,stig,crypto,fips,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:RHEL-09-672050,NIST-800-53:SC-8,NIST-800-53:SC-8(2)`
    control_objective `SC-8`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Rocky9:localhost:os-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Set system crypto policy to FIPS using update-crypto-policies --set FIPS.`

    component_id `comp-r9-os`

    impl_SC_8 `System cryptographic policy is validated to meet FIPS and organizational requirements through the crypto-policies framework.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT crypto_check
        expected_policy `FIPS`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE policy_compliant
        tool_available boolean = true
        current_policy string = `FIPS`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN crypto_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF policy_compliant
            OBJECT_REF crypto_check
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
